archive-sha256: c5a5de26d684a1a84060ad7b6131654fb2835e03fccad85059be92f8e3ffe993

Why these are vendored rather than taken from a system package: the addon has to
build on a machine that has no PipeWire development package, and the SPA format
builders it needs are static inline functions in the headers rather than
exported symbols, so `dlopen` alone cannot reach them. The library itself is
never linked and never redistributed — only these headers are checked in, and
every PipeWire function is resolved at runtime by `dlopen` against whatever the
host provides.

Scope: the two public include trees, unmodified.
  pipewire-0.3/pipewire/*.h   from src/pipewire/*.h
  spa-0.2/spa/**/*.h          from spa/include/spa/**/*.h

The tag is chosen to match the runtime library this project was developed
against (libpipewire-0.3.so.0.1005.0). PipeWire keeps its 0.3 ABI stable, so a
host with a different 1.x runtime is expected to work; a host with no PipeWire
at all is reported as an unavailable backend rather than failing to load.
